const faqs = [
  { q: 'When is the Great Migration in Kenya?', a: 'The wildebeest herds typically arrive in the Masai Mara from July and remain until October. The dramatic Mara River crossings are most frequent in August and September. Outside this window the Masai Mara still offers outstanding year-round big cat and elephant sightings.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a visa for Kenya?', a: 'Kenya replaced the tourist visa with an Electronic Travel Authorisation (eTA) in January 2024. Apply at etakenya.go.ke before travel. The eTA costs USD 30 per person and allows a 90-day stay. Most nationalities are eligible. Check current requirements before booking as the system continues to evolve.' },
  { q: 'Can I combine Kenya and Uganda in one trip?', a: 'Yes. A popular combination spends 3 to 4 days in Uganda for gorilla trekking in Bwindi, then flies to Nairobi for the Masai Mara and optionally Diani Beach. Allow 10 to 14 days for a meaningful combination of both countries. The East Africa Tourist Visa (USD 100) covers both Kenya and Uganda.' },
